# What must not reach the build context.
#
# `local/` is the line that matters: it holds the Anthropic API key and the
# personal profile seed. It is gitignored for that reason and it is excluded
# here for the same one — a key that never entered the repository should not
# enter an image that gets pushed to a public registry either. The Dockerfile
# copies named paths rather than `COPY . .`, so this is belt and braces, and
# that is the correct amount for a credential.

.git/
.github/
.venv/
.claude/
.claude-worktrees/
.claude/worktrees/
local/

# Committed artifacts for inspection, not things the app reads at runtime.
build/

# The suite brings its own Postgres and runs from a checkout; it has no job
# inside the image.
tests/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
.DS_Store

# Prose that ships in the repo rather than the image. README.md and LICENSE
# are exceptions — pyproject names them and the build needs them.
#
# `docs/` is NOT excluded, and the omission is the point: the app serves
# `docs/mcp-config.md` at /docs/ and the landing card links it, so the
# directory is runtime content in a checkout-mode image rather than prose
# about it (see the COPY in the Dockerfile). Excluding it here while the
# Dockerfile copied it is what broke the v0.1.4 build — `COPY` of an ignored
# path is not a silent no-op, it fails the build with "/docs: not found",
# which is the good outcome and the reason this is a comment and not a bug
# report. If a future change stops serving documents, delete the COPY and
# put `docs/` back.
CONTRIBUTING.md
CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
CLAUDE.md
DIRECTION.md
